    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics feels like a bridge between abstract ideas and real-world logic for me—something I find both challenging and rewarding. My parents didn’t emphasize it much in school, but my curiosity led me to explore patterns in nature or baking recipes (like converting measurements) as hobbies. It’s not my strongest subject, but I enjoy the problem-solving aspect, especially when it connects to chemistry or philosophy.",
